\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The central idea, on a real episode from the corpus (DENTEX image 127, an impacted FDI tooth 48). (a) When a grounding box is taken as an answer, the crop of that box looks authoritative and every later observation inherits its error --- here the returned box (blue) sits 0.92 box-sizes from the expert box (green; IoU 0.07). (b) VLM-DENTAL{} treats the box as a hypothesis: the policy sees a crop dominated by an upper molar, judges the box ``about one arch too high'', corrects it with one box-relative \texttt  {nudge\_crop} (orange; IoU 0.94), and answers from the corrected view. Crops are native-resolution views of the box with 30\% padding, illustrative of what the zoom tool returns rather than the canonical-view geometry of \cref  {fig:inputgeom}. Further episodes are in \cref  {fig:gallery}; the full with-tools trace of another image is dissected in \cref  {fig:evidence,fig:traces}.}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:concept}{{1}{3}{The central idea, on a real episode from the corpus (DENTEX image 127, an impacted FDI tooth 48). (a) When a grounding box is taken as an answer, the crop of that box looks authoritative and every later observation inherits its error --- here the returned box (blue) sits 0.92 box-sizes from the expert box (green; IoU 0.07). (b) \sys {} treats the box as a hypothesis: the policy sees a crop dominated by an upper molar, judges the box ``about one arch too high'', corrects it with one box-relative \texttt {nudge\_crop} (orange; IoU 0.94), and answers from the corrected view. Crops are native-resolution views of the box with 30\% padding, illustrative of what the zoom tool returns rather than the canonical-view geometry of \cref {fig:inputgeom}. Further episodes are in \cref {fig:gallery}; the full with-tools trace of another image is dissected in \cref {fig:evidence,fig:traces}}{figure.caption.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:concept@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][2][]3}}
