\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces What the tools return: the project's own tool functions, run with the arguments the policy actually chose in two released traces, on the same zoom crop. (a) A DENTEX image: the three \texttt  {window\_level} presets, an exact center/width override, \texttt  {enhance\_contrast} and bilateral \texttt  {denoise}. (b) A Tufts image: heavier denoising, two contrast factors, and \texttt  {contralateral\_compare}, which sets the region beside its mirror across the midline. The tools were applied to the 1,800\,px copy of each radiograph resized to native geometry.}}{12}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tools}{{7}{12}{What the tools return: the project's own tool functions, run with the arguments the policy actually chose in two released traces, on the same zoom crop. (a) A DENTEX image: the three \texttt {window\_level} presets, an exact center/width override, \texttt {enhance\_contrast} and bilateral \texttt {denoise}. (b) A Tufts image: heavier denoising, two contrast factors, and \texttt {contralateral\_compare}, which sets the region beside its mirror across the midline. The tools were applied to the 1,800\,px copy of each radiograph resized to native geometry}{figure.caption.12}{}}
\newlabel{fig:tools@cref}{{[figure][7][]7}{[1][9][]12}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Fixed rates, decoupled from detector accuracy.}{12}{section*.14}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The \texttt  {locate\_tooth} backend: YOLOv8m trained with 5-fold cross-validation on the combined DENTEX+Tufts pool (2{,}339 images, 46{,}808 tooth boxes; one class per FDI quadrant--position pair, target-filtered protocol). Top: in-fold target mAP50 per fold for the DENTEX-only and multi-dataset models (means 0.9508 / 0.9376). Bottom: pool composition and co-training effect (left), the held-out official DENTEX validation (best target mAP50 0.9593 at precision 0.9864 --- the deployed checkpoint) and the trace-generation guarantee (right): when a requested tooth exists in the ground truth, \texttt  {locate\_tooth} returns its exact box, and only the \emph  {displayed} copy is perturbed. Exact per-fold numbers in \cref  {app:grounding}.}}{13}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:groundingcv}{{8}{13}{The \texttt {locate\_tooth} backend: YOLOv8m trained with 5-fold cross-validation on the combined DENTEX+Tufts pool (2{,}339 images, 46{,}808 tooth boxes; one class per FDI quadrant--position pair, target-filtered protocol). Top: in-fold target mAP50 per fold for the DENTEX-only and multi-dataset models (means 0.9508 / 0.9376). Bottom: pool composition and co-training effect (left), the held-out official DENTEX validation (best target mAP50 0.9593 at precision 0.9864 --- the deployed checkpoint) and the trace-generation guarantee (right): when a requested tooth exists in the ground truth, \texttt {locate\_tooth} returns its exact box, and only the \emph {displayed} copy is perturbed. Exact per-fold numbers in \cref {app:grounding}}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\newlabel{fig:groundingcv@cref}{{[figure][8][]8}{[1][11][]13}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{No verbal cue; magnitude carries the signal.}{13}{section*.15}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The tiered perturbation mechanism and the correction loop it trains. The perturbation applies to the box shown to the policy only; offsets reuse \texttt  {nudge\_crop}'s own math; and no verbal cue marks an error, so the offset magnitude alone must carry the signal.}}{14}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{9}{14}{The tiered perturbation mechanism and the correction loop it trains. The perturbation applies to the box shown to the policy only; offsets reuse \texttt {nudge\_crop}'s own math; and no verbal cue marks an error, so the offset magnitude alone must carry the signal}{figure.caption.16}{}}
\newlabel{fig:mechanism@cref}{{[figure][9][]9}{[1][14][]14}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.6}Trace generation, verification, and decontamination}{14}{subsection.3.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:traces}{{3.6}{14}{Trace generation, verification, and decontamination}{subsection.3.6}{}}
\newlabel{sec:traces@cref}{{[subsection][6][3]3.6}{[1][14][]14}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Trace synthesis, stage 1: generation. Provider family A runs a ground-truth-directed LangGraph loop (thought, tool call, observation, repeated every turn) with real tool execution; the tiered perturbation hook perturbs only the box shown to the teacher, and the zoom monitor shows a real before/after nudge (DENTEX image 62). The unverified pool carries the real executed tool calls and corrective nudges and has no training value until verified.}}{15}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tracegen}{{10}{15}{Trace synthesis, stage 1: generation. Provider family A runs a ground-truth-directed LangGraph loop (thought, tool call, observation, repeated every turn) with real tool execution; the tiered perturbation hook perturbs only the box shown to the teacher, and the zoom monitor shows a real before/after nudge (DENTEX image 62). The unverified pool carries the real executed tool calls and corrective nudges and has no training value until verified}{figure.caption.17}{}}
\newlabel{fig:tracegen@cref}{{[figure][10][]10}{[1][15][]15}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Trace synthesis, stages 2--3: verification, decontamination, and release. Staged verification (deliberately a \emph  {different} provider family) combines a strict clinical pass with a repair-and-re-verify loop; a dual-gate leak audit and corpus assembly produce the frozen canonical release; the audit bars are measured counts. The verifier's 92 first-pass rejections span three categories --- the third (uncorrected spatial drift) exists only because the perturbation mechanism creates genuine judgment pressure.}}{16}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:traceverif}{{11}{16}{Trace synthesis, stages 2--3: verification, decontamination, and release. Staged verification (deliberately a \emph {different} provider family) combines a strict clinical pass with a repair-and-re-verify loop; a dual-gate leak audit and corpus assembly produce the frozen canonical release; the audit bars are measured counts. The verifier's 92 first-pass rejections span three categories --- the third (uncorrected spatial drift) exists only because the perturbation mechanism creates genuine judgment pressure}{figure.caption.18}{}}
\newlabel{fig:traceverif@cref}{{[figure][11][]11}{[1][15][]16}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.7}Anatomy of a trace: with tools vs.\ without}{16}{subsection.3.7}\protected@file@percent }
